  "rules": {
    "summary": "16 clubs in one table, 30 games each (15 home, 15 away), 3 points a win and 1 a draw. Teams level on points are separated by goal difference, most wins, most goals scored, head-to-head points, head-to-head goals scored, fewest disciplinary points, then a coin flip or drawing of lots; each step fully separates the teams it can, and those still level go on to the next. The top eight reach the single-elimination playoffs: quarterfinals 1 v 8, 2 v 7, 3 v 6 and 4 v 5, semifinals 1/8 v 4/5 and 2/7 v 3/6 (no reseeding), hosted by the higher seed unless its venue is unavailable, then the NWSL Championship at a predetermined venue (Audi Field, the Washington Spirit's home, on 21 November 2026). A level playoff game has two 15-minute periods of extra time, then penalties. The NWSL Shield goes to the club that tops the regular-season table.",
    "sources": [
      "https://www.nwslsoccer.com/rules-and-policies",
      "https://images.nwslsoccer.com/image/private/t_q-good/prd/hxoaampu8dszzp4ysbss.pdf",
      "https://images.nwslsoccer.com/image/private/t_q-good/prd/t44dgf8cncchutomw9no.pdf",
      "https://www.nwslsoccer.com/news/2026-nwsl-championship-presented-by-google-pixel-to-be-staged-at-audi-field-in-washington-d-c",
      "https://www.nwslsoccer.com/news/2025-nwsl-championship-presented-by-google-pixel-to-be-staged-at-paypal-park-in-san-jose-california",
      "https://www.nwslsoccer.com/news/nwsl-announces-2024-championship-to-be-held-at-cpkc-stadium-in-kansas-city",
      "https://www.nwslsoccer.com/playoffs",
      "https://www.nwslsoccer.com/standings/index"
    ]
  },
  "notes": [
    "Playoffs: the top eight qualify for single-match quarterfinals and semifinals hosted by the higher seed (1 v 8, 2 v 7, 3 v 6, 4 v 5, no reseeding); level games go to extra time, then penalties. The 2026 NWSL Championship is at Audi Field, so the Washington Spirit would play a final at home and anyone else on neutral ground.",
    "The NWSL's sixth tiebreaker, fewest disciplinary points, is not in the data; ESPN's published order is used whenever its records agree with the results.",
    "Backtested on the 2024 and 2025 seasons (FixtureDownload has no earlier NWSL feed): week-ahead match predictions score 0.220 (ranked probability score) against 0.237 for home/draw/away base rates, and playoff, top-four, Shield and title odds at a quarter, half and three quarters of each season were scored to check the strength drift."
  ],
